From: XG2010G voice bring-up <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] en75xx-isi-spi: restore validated EN7581 voice routing

The XG2010G Si32192 is reachable after the chip-SCU route is initialized
with the values observed during the successful cold-boot recovery:
0x00031000 at register 0x218 and 0x00000c01 at register 0x1d0.

Keep the full update masks so stale PCM/SPI route bits are replaced on
every probe instead of depending on a previous boot or a devmem override.
---
 src/en75xx_isi_spi.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/en75xx_isi_spi.c
+++ b/src/en75xx_isi_spi.c
@@ -132,8 +132,8 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(en7528_pcm_clk, "enable
 #define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_CLKSRC		0x218
-#define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_CLKSRC_MASK	BIT(12)
-#define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_GPIO_DEV1	BIT(12)
+#define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_CLKSRC_MASK	0x003f3300u
+#define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_GPIO_DEV1	0x00031000u
 #define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_PINMUX		0x1d0
 #define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_PINMUX_MASK	0x00000c01u
